30,2,1,talk,Shizue,,It seems that sitting close helps the new members learn and reduces the need for long notes. It's quite heartwarming.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The badge records show we arrive at very different times. Also, daylight is a major point of contention in the survey.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The billing is based on area, not people... and re-running power is quite expensive every time we change.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Oh no! Setting up every morning takes a lot of time, and those unplanned shuffles were a total mess for weeks!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"As I suspected. The noise varies significantly across the room, and adjusting the equipment for ergonomics takes days of tweaking.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Daisuke, if the cost is high, perhaps we should choose a layout that we can stick with for a long time?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"If we use a first-come system, the early arrivals always get the best spots, including the windows.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,Yes... I think we should avoid frequent changes. It seems too costly and disruptive.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Mio,,I agree with Daisuke! I can't handle spending ten minutes every morning just to get my screens working.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"If we move constantly, we lose our ergonomic settings. That is unacceptable for anyone sitting eight hours a day.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"It sounds like we all value stability, but we also want to make sure we are communicating well.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"Stability is good, but we must ensure the distribution of ""good"" seats isn't just a matter of who wakes up earliest.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I just don't want us to waste the budget on things that don't help us work better.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Mio,,But we can't just stay as we are! We've outgrown the space. We need a real plan.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,A fixed arrangement seems the most logical to avoid the chaos Mio mentioned and the physical strain I noted.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I agree that a fixed plan helps, as long as we think about who sits by whom.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"Fixed desks would solve the ""arrival time"" inequality, provided the assignment is fair.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"If it's fixed, we only pay the facilities quote once. That's much better.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Mio,,As long as we don't have to shuffle every time someone changes projects!,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,Exactly. Let's look at the options and pick the one that minimizes friction.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
